  "lab": {
    "id": "g1-l1",
    "title": "Lesson 1.1 — Switches, Routers & VLANs Revisited",
    "blurb": "Wake the deck router, split the switch into two VLANs, and route between them.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "Wake the deck router",
        "body": "Rivet: \"Cisco ports start shut down.\" Double-click `deck-rtr` to open its console. Type `enable`, then `configure terminal`. Go to `interface g0/0` and type `no shutdown`. Then `interface g0/1`, give it `ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0` and `no shutdown`. Type `end`, then `show ip interface brief` to see both ports up.",
        "objectives": [
          {
            "id": "g1l1-g00",
            "label": "deck-rtr GigabitEthernet0/0 is no longer shut down",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-rtr",
              "iface": "eth0",
              "is": {
                "shutdown": false
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-g01",
            "label": "deck-rtr GigabitEthernet0/1 is 192.168.20.1/24",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-ip",
              "device": "deck-rtr",
              "iface": "eth1",
              "cidr": "192.168.20.1/24"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-g01up",
            "label": "deck-rtr GigabitEthernet0/1 is up",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-rtr",
              "iface": "eth1",
              "is": {
                "shutdown": false
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-gw",
            "label": "astro can reach its gateway 192.168.10.1",
            "check": {
              "type": "ping",
              "from": "astro",
              "expect": "success",
              "toAddr": "192.168.10.1"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Split the deck into VLANs",
        "body": "Astro: \"Crew on one network, workshop on another.\" On `deck-sw`: `enable`, `conf t`, then `vlan 10`, `name CREW`, `vlan 20`, `name WORKSHOP`, `exit`. Put the crew ports in VLAN 10: `interface range g0/1 - 2`, `switchport access vlan 10`. Rivet's port joins VLAN 20: `interface g0/3`, `switchport access vlan 20`. The router's two cables need the same split: `interface g0/7` (to g0/0) goes in VLAN 10, `interface g0/8` (to g0/1) in VLAN 20. Check with `show vlan brief`.",
        "objectives": [
          {
            "id": "g1l1-v-astro",
            "label": "Switch port Gi0/1 (astro) is in VLAN 10",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth0",
              "is": {
                "accessVlan": 10
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-v-volt",
            "label": "Switch port Gi0/2 (volt) is in VLAN 10",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth1",
              "is": {
                "accessVlan": 10
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-v-rivet",
            "label": "Switch port Gi0/3 (rivet) is in VLAN 20",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth2",
              "is": {
                "accessVlan": 20
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-v-r0",
            "label": "Switch port Gi0/7 (router g0/0) is in VLAN 10",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth6",
              "is": {
                "accessVlan": 10
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-v-r1",
            "label": "Switch port Gi0/8 (router g0/1) is in VLAN 20",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth7",
              "is": {
                "accessVlan": 20
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-route",
            "label": "astro reaches rivet through the router",
            "check": {
              "type": "ping",
              "from": "astro",
              "expect": "success",
              "toDevice": "rivet"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-route2",
            "label": "volt reaches rivet through the router",
            "check": {
              "type": "ping",
              "from": "volt",
              "expect": "success",
              "toDevice": "rivet"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Lock the PC ports",
        "body": "Volt: \"A port that is only for a PC should say so, or a stranger's switch could talk it into carrying every VLAN.\" On `deck-sw`, set the three PC ports to access mode: `interface range g0/1 - 3`, then `switchport mode access`. `show interfaces g0/1 switchport` shows \"static access\".",
        "objectives": [
          {
            "id": "g1l1-m-astro",
            "label": "Gi0/1 is an access port",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth0",
              "is": {
                "mode": "access"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-m-volt",
            "label": "Gi0/2 is an access port",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth1",
              "is": {
                "mode": "access"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "g1l1-m-rivet",
            "label": "Gi0/3 is an access port",
            "check": {
              "type": "iface-config",
              "device": "deck-sw",
              "iface": "eth2",
              "is": {
                "mode": "access"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
